/*
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
    UIMapShared.uss
    Map marker styling  —  shared by the minimap and the world map
    Unity UIToolkit  (Unity 6.x LTS)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

    NO color literals — every colour is a --map-* token from FishMMO-Theme.uss.

    Loaded by BOTH UIMinimap.uxml and UIMap.uxml. That is the point of the file:
    the two panels draw the same markers through the same UITKMapView, and a
    per-panel copy of these rules is how the same creature ends up a different
    colour depending on which map the player is looking at.

    The type modifier classes are generated in C# from MapMarkerType — the class
    name is the enum member lowercased, prefixed with map-marker--. A type added
    to the enum without a rule here still draws, in the fallback colour below;
    it is a missing style, not a missing marker.

    Every marker is drawn as a coloured dot because the project ships no marker
    art yet. Assigning a Sprite on a MapMarker or a point of interest replaces
    the dot with that sprite, tinted by the marker's own colour, with no change
    needed here.
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
*/


/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   MARKER
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

/*
    Positioned absolutely by C#, which writes left/top in pixels and a -50%/-50% translate so those
    coordinates address the marker's centre rather than its top-left corner.
*/
.map-marker {
    position: absolute;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
}

/*
    The dot. Its size is written per-marker in C# (a landmark is larger than a note), so no width
    or height is declared here — only the shape, the outline and the fallback colour.

    The outline is not decoration. A marker is drawn over terrain of arbitrary brightness, and a
    plain coloured dot disappears against ground of a similar tone; a dark ring gives every marker
    an edge against sand and snow as well as against water.
*/
.map-marker__icon {
    border-radius: 50%;
    border-width: 1px;
    border-color: var(--shadow-text-hard);
    background-color: var(--map-npc);
    flex-shrink: 0;
}

.map-marker__label {
    margin-left: 3px;
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--text-bright);
    text-shadow: 1px 1px 2px var(--shadow-text-hard);
    white-space: nowrap;
}

/*
    A marker pinned to the frame edge because its object is outside the view. Shrunk and dimmed:
    it is a direction, not a position, and drawing it at full weight puts a permanent ring of
    bright dots around the map that competes with everything actually on it.
*/
.map-marker--clamped {
    opacity: 0.7;
}

.map-marker--clamped .map-marker__icon {
    scale: 0.75 0.75;
}


/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   MARKER TYPES
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

/*
    The player's own character. Larger and ringed in white so it is findable at a glance on a busy
    map — this is the one marker a player looks for deliberately rather than notices.
*/
.map-marker--self .map-marker__icon {
    background-color: var(--map-self);
    border-color: var(--brand-500);
    border-width: 2px;
}

.map-marker--partymember .map-marker__icon { background-color: var(--map-party); }
.map-marker--guildmember .map-marker__icon { background-color: var(--map-guild); }
.map-marker--friendlyplayer .map-marker__icon { background-color: var(--map-friendly); }
.map-marker--neutralplayer .map-marker__icon { background-color: var(--map-neutral); }
.map-marker--hostileplayer .map-marker__icon { background-color: var(--map-hostile); }

.map-marker--npc .map-marker__icon { background-color: var(--map-npc); }
.map-marker--vendor .map-marker__icon { background-color: var(--map-vendor); }
.map-marker--questgiver .map-marker__icon { background-color: var(--map-questgiver); }
.map-marker--trainer .map-marker__icon { background-color: var(--map-trainer); }
.map-marker--service .map-marker__icon { background-color: var(--map-service); }
.map-marker--resource .map-marker__icon { background-color: var(--map-resource); }
.map-marker--enemy .map-marker__icon { background-color: var(--map-enemy); }
.map-marker--interactable .map-marker__icon { background-color: var(--map-interactable); }
.map-marker--teleporter .map-marker__icon { background-color: var(--map-teleporter); }

/*
    Landmarks and notes are squared off rather than round. They are places on the map rather than
    things in the world, and the shape difference separates them from the creature markers at a
    size where colour alone does not.
*/
.map-marker--landmark .map-marker__icon {
    background-color: var(--map-landmark);
    border-radius: 2px;
}

.map-marker--note .map-marker__icon {
    background-color: var(--map-note);
    border-radius: 2px;
}
